The Gujarat Money-Lenders Act, 201I
[201] : Guj. 14
CHAPTER XMISCELLANEOUS
51. Every officer of the Govemment when acting or purporting to actin pursuance ofthe provisions of this Act or the rules made thereunder shallbe deemed to be public servant within the meaning of section 2i of the ororrlrolndian Penal Code.
52. No suit, prosecution or other legal proceedings shall lie against theRegistrar General, Registrar, Assistant Registrar or any omcer or employeesubordinate to him appointed under section 3 or any person acting on hisauthority, in respect of anythir:g which is in good faith done or purported tobe done by him in pusuance of the provisions of this Act, or rules madethereunder or any insructions, for carryigg.out the purposes of this Act.
53. Nothing in this Act shall affect any of the provisions of any lawwhich may be in force in any part of the State relating to relief of agricultualindebtedness and no Court shall entertaiq or proceed under this Act withany suit or proceeding relating to any loan in respect of which debtadjustment proceedings can be taken under the said Act, or as the case maybe, the said law.
54. Whenever a copy of any dricument from the record of anyapplication, inquiry or appeal under this Act is requted by any party to suchapplication, inquiry or appeal, it may be granted on payment of such fees asmay be prcscribed by the State Government.
55. (1) The State Government may, by notifcation n the OfuialGazette, make niJes generally for carrying out the purposes of this Act.
(2) In particular and without prejudice to the generality ofthe foregoingprovision, such nrles may provide for a1l or any of the following matters:-
(a) the form of the register of Money-Lenders to be maintained by theRegistrar under section 4;
(b) the form of application for registration under sub-section (1) ofsection 6; the other particulars of such application, under sub-section (2);
(c) the form of certificate of registration, the conditions of regisnationand fees for registation and the ma::ner of payment thereof under sub-section (1) of section 7;
