The Gujarat Money-Lenders Act, 2011
56. The State Govemment may, by general or special order io bepublished in the Oficial Gazette, exempt any Money-Lender or cl8s ofMoney-Lenders from all or any of the provisions of this Act subject to suchconditions and for such period as may be sirecified in such order.
[2011 : Guj. 14
Provisions of 57. Nothing in this Act shall affect the operation of the Gujarat Rural Gui. 3s orGuj.35-ot 1976 Debtors Relief A ct 1976. re76'oot to affecl
Repeal andsavings.
58.(1) The Bombay Money-Lenders Act 1946 is hereby repealed.
)O(Xl ofl947.
(2) Notwithstanding such repeal of the Act refer to in sub-section (l)(hereinafter in this section refer to as the "said Act")-
(a) any license issued under the said Act and validly in forceimmediately before the appointed day shall be deemed to be theregistration issued under this Act, and
(b) any appointnent, notiication, order, nrle, form, notice orregister nade, issued or maintained under the said Act shall, so faras it is not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act continue ilforce and be deemed to have been made, issued or maintained underthe provisions of this Ac! unless 4nd until it is superseded by a::yappoinment, notification, order, rule, form, notice or register made,issued or maintained under the provisions ofthis Act.
(3) A-ny other thing done or action taken under the said Act, so far asit is not inconsistent ,with the provisions of this Act, shall be deemed tobave been done or taken under the corresponding provisions of this Act andshall continue in 1o."9 accordingly, unless and until superseded by any thingdone or any action taken under this Act.
Govemment Press, Vadodara-

